{
  "title": "26: al-Shoa'raa الشعراء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nطٰسٓمّٓ‏(1)\nTaa Sim Meem. \nTaa Sim Meem. \nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(2)\nTILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE MOBEEN.\nThese are the verses of the Book that makes (things) clear. \nلَعَلَّكَ بَاخِعٌ نَّفْسَكَ اَلَّا يَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(3)\nLAA’ALLAKA BAAKHEA’UN NNAFSAKA ALLAA YAKOONOOA MUMENEENA.\nPerhaps you will kill yourself with grief because they do not believe. \nاِنْ نَّشَاْ نُنَزِّلْ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اٰيَةً فَظَلَّتْ اَعْنَاقُهُمْ لَهَا خٰضِعِيْنَ‏(4)\nIN NASHAA NUNAZZEL A’LAYHIM MENAL SAMAAA-E AAYATAL FAZALLAT AAA’NAAQUHUM LAHAA KHAAZEE’EENA.\nIf We please, We should send down upon them a sign from the heaven so that their necks should stoop to it. \nوَمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرٍ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ مُحْدَثٍ اِلَّا كَانُوْا عَنْهُ مُعْرِضِيْنَ‏(5)\nWA MAA YAATEEHIM MIN ZEKRIN MENAL RAHMAANIR MUHDASIN ILLAA KAANOO A’NHO MOA’REZEEN.\nAnd there does not come to them a new reminder from the Beneficent Allah but they turn aside from it. \nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْا فَسَيَاْتِيْهِمْ اَنْۢبٰٓؤُا مَا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(6)\nFAQAD KAZZABOO FASAYAATEEHEM AANBAAAUA MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nSo they have indeed rejected (the truth), therefore the news of that which they mock shall soon come to them. \nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلَى الْاَرْضِ كَمْ اَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍ كَرِيْمٍ‏(7)\nAWALAM YARAW ELAL ARZE KAM AANBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIN KAREEM.\nDo they not see the earth, how many of every noble kind We have caused to grow in it? \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(8)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nMost surely there is a sign in that, but most of them will not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(9)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nوَاِذْ نَادٰى رَبُّكَ مُوْسٰۤى اَنِ ائْتِ الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWA IZ NAADAA RABBOKA MOOSAA SAALEHAN ATE QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when your Lord called out to Musa, saying: Go to the unjust people, \nقَوْمَ فِرْعَوْنَ‌ؕ اَلَا يَتَّقُوْنَ‌‏(11)\nQAWMA FIR-A’WN ALAA YATTAQOON.\nThe people of Firon: Will they not guard (against evil)? \nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْنِؕ‏(12)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE AKHAAFO AN YYUKAZZEBOONE.\nHe said: O my Lord! surely I fear that they will reject me; \nوَيَضِيْقُ صَدْرِىْ وَلَا يَنْطَلِقُ لِسَانِىْ فَاَرْسِلْ اِلٰى هٰرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWAYAZEEQU SADREAA WA LAA YANTALEQU LESAANEAA FAARSEL ELAA AALO.\nAnd by breast straitens, and my tongue is not eloquent, therefore send Thou to Haroun (to help me); \nوَلَهُمْ عَلَىَّ ذَنْۢبٌ فَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّقْتُلُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(14)\nWA LAHUM A’LAYYA ZANBUN FA AKHAAFO AN YAQTOLOON.\nAnd they have a crime against me, therefore I fear that they may slay me. \nقَالَ كَلَّا‌ ۚ فَاذْهَبَا بِاٰيٰتِنَآ‌ اِنَّا مَعَكُمْ مُّسْتَمِعُوْنَ‏(15)\nQAALA KALLAA FAAZHABAA BE-AAYAATENAA INNAA MA-A’KUM MMUSTAMEU’OONA.\nHe said: By no means, so go you both with Our signs; surely We are with you, hearing; \nفَاْتِيَا فِرْعَوْنَ فَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّا رَسُوْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(16)\nFAATEEA FIR-A’WNA FAQOOLAA INNAA RASOOLAL RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nThen come to Firon and say: Surely we are the apostles of the Lord of the worlds: \nاَنْ اَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(17)\nAN AARSEL MAA’ANAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nThen send with us the children of Israel. \nقَالَ اَلَمْ نُرَبِّكَ فِيْنَا وَلِيْدًا وَّلَبِثْتَ فِيْنَا مِنْ عُمُرِكَ سِنِيْنَۙ‏(18)\nQAALA ALAM NURABBEKA FEENAA WALEEDAN WWALABESTA FEENAA MIN U’UMUREKA SENEEN.\n(Firon) said: Did we not bring you up as a child among us, and you tarried among us for (many) years of your life? \nوَفَعَلْتَ فَعْلَتَكَ الَّتِىْ فَعَلْتَ وَاَنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(19)\nWAFAA’ALTA FAA’LATAKA LATEE FAA’ALTA WA ANTA MENAL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd you did (that) deed of yours which you did, and you are one of the ungrateful. \nقَالَ فَعَلْتُهَاۤ اِذًا وَّاَنَا مِنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَؕ‏(20)\nQAALA FAA’ALTUHAA EZAL WWAANAA MENAL AZ-ZAALLEENA.\nHe said: I did it then while I was of those unable to see the right course; \nفَفَرَرْتُ مِنْكُمْ لَمَّا خِفْتُكُمْ فَوَهَبَ لِىْ رَبِّىْ حُكْمًا وَّجَعَلَنِىْ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(21)\nFAFARARTU MINKUM LAMMAA KHEFTUKUM FAWAHABA LEE RABBEE HUKMAWN WWAJAA’ALANEAA MENAL MURSALEEN.\nSo I fled from you when I feared you, then my Lord granted me wisdom and made me of the apostles; \nوَتِلْكَ نِعْمَةٌ تَمُنُّهَا عَلَىَّ اَنْ عَبَّدْتَّ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(22)\nWA TILKAL NEA’MATUN TAMUNNUHAA A’LAYYA AN A’ABBADTTA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nAnd is it a favor of which you remind me that you have enslaved the children of Israel? \nقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(23)\nQAALA FIRA’WNO WA MAA RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nFiron said: And what is the Lord of the worlds? \nقَالَ رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَاؕ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّوْقِنِيْنَ‏(24)\nQAALA RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHUMAA IN KUNTUM MOOQENEEN.\nHe said: The Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, if you would be sure. \nقَالَ لِمَنْ حَوْلَهٗۤ اَلَا تَسْتَمِعُوْنَ‏(25)\nQAALA LEMAN-Y HAWLAHU ALAA TASTAMEU’OONA.\n(Firon) said to those around him: Do you not hear? \nقَالَ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA RABBOKUM WA RABBO AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\nHe said: Your Lord and the Lord of your fathers of old. \nقَالَ اِنَّ رَسُوْلَكُمُ الَّذِىْۤ اُرْسِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ لَمَجْنُوْنٌ‏(27)\nQAALA INNAL RASOOLAKUMU LAZEE AURSELA ELAYKUM LAMAJNOONUN.\nSaid he: Most surely your Apostle who is sent to you is mad. \nقَالَ رَبُّ الْمَشْرِقِ وَالْمَغْرِبِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(28)\nQAALA RABBUL MASHREQE WAL MAGHREBE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA IN KUNTUM TA’QELOON.\nHe said: The Lord of the east and the west and what is between them, if you understand. \nقَالَ لَئِنِ اتَّخَذْتَ اِلٰهًا غَيْرِىْ لَاَجْعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ الْمَسْجُوْنِيْنَ‏(29)\nQAALA LAENE ATTAKHAZTA ELAAHANW GHAYREE LAAJA’ALANNAKA MENAL AL-MASJOONEENA.\nSaid he: If you will take a god besides me, I will most certainly make you one of the imprisoned. \nقَالَ اَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكَ بِشَىْءٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(30)\nQAALA LAW JE’TOKA BE-SHAY-IM MOBEEN.\nHe said: What! even if I bring to you something manifest? \nقَالَ فَاْتِ بِهٖۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(31)\nQAALA FAATE BEHI IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nSaid he: Bring it then, if you are of the truthful ones. \n‌فَاَ لْقٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ ۖ ‌‌ۚ‏(32)\nFA-ALQEEHE LQAA A’ASAAHU FA-EZAA HEYA SUA’BAANUN MOBEEN.\nSo he cast down his rod, and lo! it was an obvious serpent, \nوَّنَزَعَ يَدَهٗ فَاِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَ‏(33)\nWWANAZAA’A YADAH FA-EZAA HEYA BAYZAAU LELNNAAZEREENA.\nAnd he drew forth his hand, and lo! it appeared white to the onlookers. \nقَالَ لِلْمَلَاِ حَوْلَهٗۤ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(34)\nQAALA LIL-MALAA HAWLAHU INNAL HAAZAA LASAAHERUN A’LEEM.\n(Firon) said to the chiefs around him: Most surely this is a skillful magician, \nيُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّخْرِجَكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهٖ ‌ۖ  فَمَاذَا تَاْمُرُوْنَ‌‏(35)\nYYUREEDU AN YYUKHREJAKUM MIN AARZEKUM BESEHREH FA MAA TAAMUROONA.\nWho desires to turn you out of your land with his magic; what is it then that you advise? \nقَالُوْۤا اَرْجِهْ وَاَخَاهُ وَابْعَثْ فِى الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِيْنَۙ‏(36)\nQAALOO AARJEH WAAKHAAHU WAB A’S FIL AL-MADAAENE HAASHEREENA.\nThey said: Give him and his brother respite and send heralds into the cities \nيَاْتُوْكَ بِكُلِّ سَحَّارٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(37)\nYAATOOKA BEKULLE SAHHAARIN A’LEEM.\nThat they should bring to you every skillful magician. \nفَجُمِعَ السَّحَرَةُ لِمِيْقَاتِ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍۙ‏(38)\nFAJUMEA’A AS-SAHARATU LE-MEEQAATE YAWMIN MA’LOOM.\nSo the magicians were gathered together at the appointed time on the fixed day, \nوَّقِيْلَ لِلنَّاسِ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّجْتَمِعُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWWAQEELA LIN-NAASE HAL ANTUM MMUJTAMEU’OONA.\nAnd it was said to the people: Will you gather together? \nلَعَلَّنَا نَتَّبِعُ السَّحَرَةَ اِنْ كَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(40)\nLAA’ALLANAA NATTA-BE-O’ AS-SAHARATA IN KAANOO HOMUL AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nHaply we may follow the magicians, if they are the vanquishers. \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ قَالُوْا لِفِرْعَوْنَ اَئِنَّ لَنَا لَاَجْرًا اِنْ كُنَّا نَحْنُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(41)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AS-SAHARATU QAALOO LE-FIR-A’WNA AAENNA LANAA LAAJRAN IN KUNNAA NAHNO AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nAnd when the magicians came, they said to Firon: Shall we get a reward if we are the vanquishers? \nقَالَ نَعَمْ وَاِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ‏(42)\nQAALA NAA’AM WA INNAKUM EZAL LAMENAZ MOQARRABEEN.\nHe said: Yes, and surely you will then be of those who are made near. \nقَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰۤى اَلْقُوْا مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ مُّلْقُوْنَ‏(43)\nQAALA LAHUM MOOSAA AALQOOA MAA ANTUM MMULQOONA.\nMusa said to them: Cast what you are going to cast. \nفَاَلْقَوْا حِبَالَهُمْ وَعِصِيَّهُمْ وَقَالُوْا بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(44)\nFAALQAWA HEBAALAHUM WAE’ESEEHUM WA QAALOO BEE’EZZATE FIR-A’WNA INNAA LANAHNU GHAALEBOON.\nSo they cast down their cords and their rods and said: By Firon's power, we shall most surely be victorious. \nفَاَ لْقٰى مُوْسٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَاْفِكُوْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(45)\nFA-ALQEEHE LQAA MOOSAA A’ASAAHU FA-EZAA HEYA TALQAFU MAA YAAFEKOONA.\nThen Musa cast down his staff and lo! it swallowed up the lies they told. \nفَاُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سٰجِدِيْنَۙ‏(46)\nFA ULQEYA AS-SAHARATU SAAJEDEENA.\nAnd the magicians were thrown down prostrate; \nقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(47)\nQAALOO AAMANNAA BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThey said: We believe in the Lord of the worlds: \nرَبِّ مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(48)\nRABBE MOOSAA WA AALO.\nThe Lord of Musa and Haroun. \nقَالَ اٰمَنْتُمْ لَهٗ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّهٗ لَكَبِيْرُكُمُ الَّذِىْ عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ‌ۚ فَلَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ لَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ وَّلَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(49)\nQAALA AAMANTUM LAHU QABLA AN AAAZANA LAKUM INNAHU LAKABEERUKUMU LAZEE A’ALLAMAKUMU SEHR FALASAWFA TA’LAMOON LAAQATTEA’ANNA AAYDEEKUM WAARJULAKUM MIN KHELAAFIN WWALAASALLEBANNAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nSaid he: You believe in him before I give you permission; most surely he is the chief of you who taught you the magic, so you shall know: certainly I will cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides, and certainly I will crucify you all. \nقَالُوْا لَا ضَيْرَ‌ اِنَّاۤ اِلٰى رَبِّنَا مُنْقَلِبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(50)\nQAALOO LAA ZAYRA INNAA ELAA RABBENAA MUNQALEBOONA.\nThey said: No harm; surely to our Lord we go back; \nاِنَّا نَطْمَعُ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ لَنَا رَبُّنَا خَطٰيٰنَاۤ اَنْ كُنَّاۤ اَوَّلَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(51)\nINNAA NATMAU’U AN YAGHFERAL LANAA RABBONAA KHATAAYAANAA AN KUNNAA AWWALA AL-MUMENEENA.\nSurely we hope that our Lord will forgive us our wrongs because we are the first of the believers. \nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْۤ اِنَّكُمْ مُّتَّبَعُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA AN AASRE BE-E’BAADEE INNAKUM MUTTABA-O’ONA.\nAnd We revealed to Musa, saying: Go away with My servants travelling by night, surely you will be pursued. \nفَاَرْسَلَ فِرْعَوْنُ فِى الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nFA ARSALA FIRA’WNO FIL AL-MADAAENE HAASHEREENA.\nSo Firon sent heralds into the cities; \nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ لَشِرْذِمَةٌ قَلِيْلُوْنَۙ‏(54)\nINNAL HAAOOLAAA-E LASHERZEMATUN QALEELOONA.\nMost surely these are a small company; \nوَاِنَّهُمْ لَنَا لَغَآئِظُوْنَۙ‏(55)\nWA INNAHUM LANAA LAGHAAEZOONA.\nAnd most surely they have enraged us; \nوَاِنَّا لَجَمِيْعٌ حٰذِرُوْنَؕ‏(56)\nWA INNAA LAJAMEEA’UN HAAZEROONA.\nAnd most surely we are a vigilant multitude. \nفَاَخْرَجْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(57)\nFAAKHRAJNAAHUM MIN JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nSo We turned them out of gardens and springs, \nوَّكُنُوْزٍ وَّمَقَامٍ كَرِيْمٍۙ‏(58)\nWWAKUNOOZIN WA MAQAAMIN KAREEM.\nAnd treasures and goodly dwellings, \nكَذٰلِكَؕ وَاَوْرَثْنٰهَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(59)\nKA-ZAALEK WA AWRASNAAHAA BANEE AESRAAEELA.\nEven so. And We gave them as a heritage to the children of Israel. \nفَاَ تْبَعُوْهُمْ مُّشْرِقِيْنَ‏(60)\nFA-ALQEEHE TBAU’OOHUM MMUSHREQEENA.\nThen they pursued them at sunrise. \nفَلَمَّا تَرَآءَ الْجَمْعٰنِ قَالَ اَصْحٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِنَّا لَمُدْرَكُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(61)\nFALAMMAA TARAAA AL-JAMA’AANE QAALA ASHAABUN MOOSAA INNAA LAMUDRAKOONA.\nSo when the two hosts saw each other, the companions of Musa cried out: Most surely we are being overtaken. \nقَالَ كَلَّا‌‌ ۚ اِنَّ مَعِىَ رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(62)\nQAALA KALLAA INNAL MA-E’YA RABBEE SAYAHDEENE.\nHe said: By no means; surely my Lord is with me: He will show me a way out. \nفَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنِ اضْرِبْ بِّعَصَاكَ الْبَحْرَ‌ؕ فَانْفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَالطَّوْدِ الْعَظِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(63)\nFAAWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA SAALEHAN AZREB BE-A’SAAKAL AL-BAHRA FAANFALAQA FA KAANA KULLO FERQIN KAALTTAWDE A’ZEEM.\nThen We revealed to Musa: Strike the sea with your staff. So it had cloven asunder, and each part was like a huge mound. \nوَاَزْلَفْنَا ثَمَّ الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(64)\nWAAZLAFNAA SUMMA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nAnd We brought near, there, the others. \nوَاَنْجَيْنَا مُوْسٰى وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(65)\nWA ANJAYNAL MOOSAA WA MAN MMAA’AH AJMA-E’ENA.\nAnd We saved Musa and those with him, all of them. \nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ؕ‏(66)\nSUMMA AAGHRAQNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We drowned the others. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً ‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(67)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nMost surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(68)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‌ۘ‏(69)\nWAATLU A’LAYHIM NABAA IBRAAHEEMA.\nAnd recite to them the story of Ibrahim. \nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(70)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA TA’BODOONA.\nWhen he said to his father and his people: What do you worship? \nقَالُوْا نَعْبُدُ اَصْنَامًا فَنَظَلُّ لَهَا عٰكِفِيْنَ‏(71)\nQAALOO NA’BODO AASNAAMAN FANAZALLU LAHAA A’AAKEFEENA.\nThey said: We worship idols, so we shall be their votaries. \nقَالَ هَلْ يَسْمَعُوْنَكُمْ اِذْ تَدْعُوْنَۙ‏(72)\nQAALA HAL YASMAU’OONAKUM IZ TADU’OONA.\nHe said: Do they hear you when you call? \nاَوْ يَنْفَعُوْنَكُمْ اَوْ يَضُرُّوْنَ‏(73)\nAW YANFAU’OONAKUM AW YAZURROONA.\nOr do they profit you or cause you harm? \nقَالُوْا بَلْ وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا كَذٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(74)\nQAALOO BAL WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA KAZAALEKA YAF-A’LOON.\nThey said: Nay, we found our fathers doing so. \nقَالَ اَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(75)\nQAALA AFA-RA-AYTUM MAA KUNTUM TA’BODOONA.\nHe said: Have you then considered what you have been worshipping: \nاَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمُ الْاَقْدَمُوْنَ ‌ۖ ‏(76)\nANTUM WAABAAUKUMU AL-AAQDAMOONA.\nYou and your ancient sires. \nفَاِنَّهُمْ عَدُوٌّ لِّىْۤ اِلَّا رَبَّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(77)\nFA INNAHUM A’DUWWUM LEE ILLAA LAZEE HARRAMAHAA A’ALAMEEN.\nSurely they are enemies to me, but not (so) the Lord of the worlds; \nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَنِىْ فَهُوَ يَهْدِيْنِۙ‏(78)\nLAZEE KHALAQANEAA FAHOWA YAHDEENE.\nWho created me, then He has shown me the way: \nوَ الَّذِىْ هُوَ يُطْعِمُنِىْ وَيَسْقِيْنِۙ‏(79)\nWA LAZEE HOWA YUTE’EMUNEAA WAYASQEENE.\nAnd He Who gives me to eat and gives me to drink: \nوَاِذَا مَرِضْتُ فَهُوَ يَشْفِيْنِ ۙ‏(80)\nWA EZAA MAREZTU FAHOWA YASHFEENE.\nAnd when I am sick, then He restores me to health \nوَالَّذِىْ يُمِيْتُنِىْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيْنِۙ‏(81)\nWAL LAZEE YUMEETUNEAA SUMMA YUHYEENE.\nAnd He Who will cause me to die, then give me life; \nوَالَّذِىْۤ اَطْمَعُ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ لِىْ خَطِٓیْئَتِىْ يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِ ؕ‏(82)\nWAL LAZEE AATMAU’U AN YAGHFERAL LEE KHATEAAATEAA YAWMA DEENE.\nAnd Who, I hope, will forgive me my mistakes on the day of judgment. \nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ حُكْمًا وَّاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِالصّٰلِحِيْنَۙ‏(83)\nRABBE HAB LEE HUKMAWN WWAALHEQNEAA BE-SAALEHEEN.\nMy Lord: Grant me wisdom, and join me with the good \nوَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(84)\nWA A’L LEE LESAANA SEDQIN FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd ordain for me a goodly mention among posterity \nوَاجْعَلْنِىْ مِنْ وَّرَثَةِ جَنَّةِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(85)\nWAAJA’ALNEAA MIN WWARASATE JANNATE NA-E’EM.\nAnd make me of the heirs of the garden of bliss \nوَاغْفِرْ لِاَبِىْۤ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَۙ‏(86)\nFIRLANAA LE-ABEE INNAHU KAANA MENAL ZAAL-LEEN.\nAnd forgive my father, for surely he is of those who have gone astray; \nوَلَا تُخْزِنِىْ يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُوْنَۙ‏(87)\nWA LAA TUKHZENEAA YAWMA YUB-A’SOON.\nAnd disgrace me not on the day when they are raised \nيَوْمَ لَا يَنْفَعُ مَالٌ وَّلَا بَنُوْنَۙ‏(88)\nYAWMA LAA YANFAU’N MAALUN WA LAA BANOONA.\nThe day on which property will not avail, nor sons \nاِلَّا مَنْ اَتَى اللّٰهَ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍؕ‏(89)\nILLAA MAN AATAA LAAHA BEQALBIN SALEEMIN.\nExcept him who comes to Allah with a heart free (from evil). \nوَاُزْلِفَتِ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(90)\nWAAZLEFATE JANNATO LILMUTTAQEEN.\nAnd the garden shall be brought near for those who guard (against evil), \nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِلْغٰوِيْنَۙ‏(91)\nWABURREZATE EZAL JAHEEMO LIL-GHAAWEENA.\nAnd the hell shall be made manifest to the erring ones, \nوَقِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَيْنَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(92)\nWA QEELAD LAHUM AYNAMAA KUNTUM TA’BODOONA.\nAnd it shall be said to them: Where are those that you used to worship; \nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِؕ هَلْ يَنْصُرُوْنَكُمْ اَوْ يَنْتَصِرُوْنَؕ‏(93)\nMIN DOONIL LAAH HAL YANSUROONAKUM AW YANTASEROONA.\nBesides Allah? Can they help you or yet help themselves? \nفَكُبْكِبُوْا فِيْهَا هُمْ وَالْغَاوٗنَۙ‏(94)\nFAKUBKEBOOA FEEHAA HUM WAL GHAAWNA.\nSo they shall be thrown down into it, they and the erring ones, \nوَجُنُوْدُ اِبْلِيْسَ اَجْمَعُوْنَؕ‏(95)\nWA JONOODUS AEBLEESA AAJMAU’OONA.\nAnd the hosts of the Shaitan, all. \nقَالُوْا وَهُمْ فِيْهَا يَخْتَصِمُوْنَۙ‏(96)\nQAALOO WA HUM FEEHAA YAKHTASEMOON.\nThey shall say while they contend therein: \nتَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنَّا لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(97)\nTAALLLAAHE IN KUNNAA LAFEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nBy Allah! we were certainly in manifest error, \nاِذْ نُسَوِّيْكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(98)\nIZ NUSAWYKUM BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhen we made you equal to the Lord of the worlds; \nوَمَاۤ اَضَلَّنَاۤ اِلَّا الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(99)\nWA MAA AAZALLANAA ILLAA MUJREMOON.\nAnd none but the guilty led us astray; \nفَمَا لَنَا مِنْ شٰفِعِيْنَۙ‏(100)\nFAMAA LANAA MIN SHAAFEE’EENA.\nSo we have no intercessors, \nوَلَا صَدِيْقٍ حَمِيْمٍ‏(101)\nWA LAA SADEEQIN HAMEEMIN.\nNor a true friend; \nفَلَوْ اَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةً فَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(102)\nFA LAW ANNAL LANAA KARRATAN FANAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nBut if we could but once return, we would be of the believers. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nMost surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(104)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ نُوْحِۨالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(105)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO NOOHEALMURSALEENA.\nThe people of Nuh rejected the apostles. \nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ نُوْحٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(106)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM NOOHUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen their brother Nuh said to them: Will you not guard (against evil)? \nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(107)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nSurely I am a faithful apostle to you; \nفَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَ اَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(108)\nFAT-TAQUN LAAHA WA AATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me \nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(109)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I do not ask you any reward for it; my reward is only with the Lord of the worlds: \nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ ؕ‏(110)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nSo guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me. \nقَالُوْۤا اَنُؤْمِنُ لَكَ وَاتَّبَعَكَ الْاَرْذَلُوْنَؕ‏(111)\nQAALOO A-NOAMENO LAKA WAATTABAA’AKA AL-AARZALOONA.\nThey said: Shall we believe in you while the meanest follow you? \nقَالَ وَمَا عِلْمِىْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(112)\nQAALA WA MAA E’ELMEAA BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nHe said: And what knowledge have I of what they do? \nاِنْ حِسَابُهُمْ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّىْ‌ لَوْ تَشْعُرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(113)\nIN HESAABUHUM ILLAA A’LAA RABBEE LAW TASH-O’ROON.\nTheir account is only with my Lord, if you could perceive \nوَمَاۤ اَنَا بِطَارِدِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(114)\nWA MAA ANAA BETAAREDE MOAMENEEN.\nAnd I am not going to drive away the believers; \nاِنْ اَنَا اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌؕ‏(115)\nIN ANAA ILLAA NAZEERUM MMUBEENUN.\nI am naught but a plain warner. \nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ يٰنُوْحُ لَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمَرْجُوْمِيْنَؕ‏(116)\nQAALOO LAIL LAM TANTAHE YAANOOHU LATAKOONANNA MENAL AL-MARJOOMEENA.\nThey said: If you desist not, O Nuh, you shall most certainly be of those stoned to death. \nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنَّ قَوْمِىْ كَذَّبُوْنِ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(117)\nQAALA RABBE INNAL QAWMEE KAZZABOONE.\nHe said: My Lord! Surely my people give me the lie! \nفَافْتَحْ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ فَتْحًا وَّنَجِّنِىْ وَمَنْ مَّعِىَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(118)\nFAAFTAH BAYNEE WA BAYNAHUM FATHAN WWANAJJENEAA WA MAN MA-E’YA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nTherefore judge Thou between me and them with a (just) judgment, and deliver me and those who are with me of the believers. \nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(119)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA MAN MMAA’AH FIL FULKE MASH-HOON.\nSo We delivered him and those with him in the laden ark. \nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا بَعْدُ الْبٰقِيْنَؕ‏(120)\nSUMMA AAGHRAQNAA BA’DO AL-BAAQEENA.\nThen We drowned the rest afterwards \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(121)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nMost surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(122)\nWA INNAL RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nكَذَّبَتْ عَادُ اۨلْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ‌ۖ ‌ۚ‏(123)\nKAZZABAT A’AADU MURSALEEN.\nAd gave the lie to the apostles. \nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ هُوْدٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(124)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM HOODUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen their brother Hud said to them: Will you not guard (against evil)? \nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌ‌ۙ‏(125)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nSurely I am a faithful apostle to you; \nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(126)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me: \nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(127)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I do not ask you any reward for it; surely my reward is only with the Lord of the worlds \nاَتَبْنُوْنَ بِكُلِّ رِيْعٍ اٰيَةً تَعْبَثُوْنَۙ‏(128)\nAATABNOONA BEKULLE REEA’IN AAYATAL TAA’BASOONA.\nDo you build on every height a monument? Vain is it that you do: \nوَ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(129)\nWA TATTAKHEZOONA MASAANEA’A LA-A’LLAKUM TAKHLUDOONA.\nAnd you make strong fortresses that perhaps you may \nوَاِذَا بَطَشْتُمْ بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(130)\nWA EZAA BATASHTUM BATASHTUM JABBAAREENA.\nAnd when you lay hands (on men) you lay hands (like) tyrants; \nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(131)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nSo guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me \nوَاتَّقُوْا الَّذِىْۤ اَمَدَّكُمْ بِمَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(132)\nWAT TAQOO LAZEE AAMADDAKUM BEMAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd be careful of (your duty to) Him Who has given you abundance of what you know. \nاَمَدَّكُمْ بِاَنْعَامٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ ‌ۚۙ‏(133)\nAAMADDAKUM BEAANA’AAMIN WWABANEENA.\nHe has given you abundance of cattle and children \nوَجَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍ‌ۚ‏(134)\nWA JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nAnd gardens and fountains; \nاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍؕ‏(135)\nINNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’AZEEMIN.\nSurely I fear for you the chastisement of a grievous day \nقَالُوْا سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَوَعَظْتَ اَمْ لَمْ تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْوٰعِظِيْنَۙ‏(136)\nQAALOO SAWAAA-UN A’LAYNAA AAWAA’AZTA AM LAM TAKUN MENAL AL-WAAE’EZEENA.\nThey said: It is the same to us whether you admonish or are not one of the admonishers \nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا خُلُقُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(137)\nIN HAAZAA ILLAA KHULUQU AWWALEEN.\nThis is naught but a custom of the ancients; \nوَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(138)\nWA MAA NAHNO BEMUA’AZZABEENA.\nAnd we are not going to be punished. \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاَيَةً‌ ؕ وَ مَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(139)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FAAHLAKNAAHUM INNAL FEE ZAALEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nSo they gave him the lie, then We destroyed them. Most surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(140)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(141)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO MURSALEEN.\nSamood gave the lie to the apostles \nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ صٰلِحٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(142)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM SAALEHUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen their brother Salih said to them: Will you not guard (against evil)? \nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(143)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nSurely I am a faithful apostle to you \nفَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(144)\nFAT-TAQUN LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me: \nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(145)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I do not ask you any reward for it; my reward is only with the Lord of the worlds: \nاَتُتْرَكُوْنَ فِىْ مَا هٰهُنَاۤ اٰمِنِيْنَۙ‏(146)\nAATUTRAKOONA FEE MAA HAAHUNAA AAMENEENA.\nWill you be left secure in what is here; \nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(147)\nFEE JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nIn gardens and fountains, \nوَّزُرُوْعٍ وَّنَخْلٍ طَلْعُهَا هَضِيْمٌ‌ۚ‏(148)\nWA ZOROO-I’NW WWANAKHLIN TALU’UHAA HAZEEMUN.\nAnd cornfields and palm-trees having fine spadices? \nوَتَنْحِتُوْنَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا فٰرِهِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(149)\nWATANHETOONA MENAL JEBAALE BUYOOTAN FAAREHEENA.\nAnd you hew houses out of the mountains exultingly; \nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(150)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me; \nوَلَا تُطِيْعُوْۤا اَمْرَ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَۙ‏(151)\nWA LAA TO-TEE-O’O AAMRA MUSREFEEN.\nAnd do not obey the bidding of the extravagant, \nالَّذِيْنَ يُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَ لَا يُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(152)\nLAZEENA YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE WA LAA LAA YUSLEHOON.\nWho make mischief in the land and do not act aright. \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(153)\nQAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MENAL AL-MUSAHHAREENA.\nThey said: You are only of the deluded ones; \nمَاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا ‌ ۖۚ فَاْتِ بِاٰيَةٍ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(154)\nMAA ANTA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA FAATE BE-AAYATIL IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nYou are naught but a mortal like ourselves; so bring a sign if you are one of the truthful. \nقَالَ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَّلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍ‌ۚ‏(155)\nQAALA HAAZEHI NAAQATUN LLAHAA SHERBUN WWALAKUM SHERBU YAWMIN MA’LOOM.\nHe said: This is a she-camel; she shall have her portion of water, and you have your portion of water on an appointed time; \nوَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(156)\nWA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOOO-IN FAYAAKHUZAKUM A’ZAABO YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nAnd do not touch her with evil, lest the punishment of a grievous day should overtake you. \nفَعَقَرُوْهَا فَاَصْبَحُوْا نٰدِمِيْنَۙ‏(157)\nFA-A’QAROOHAA FA-ASBAHOO NAADEMEENA.\nBut they hamstrung her, then regretted; \nفَاَخَذَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(158)\nTOOFAANO A’ZAAB INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nSo the punishment overtook them. Most surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(159)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ اۨلْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(160)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO LOOTIM MURSALEEN.\nThe people of Lut gave the lie to the apostles. \nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ لُوْطٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(161)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AAKHOOHUM LOOT ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen their brother Lut said to them: Will you not guard (against evil)? \nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(162)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nSurely I am a faithful apostle to you; \nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(163)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me: \nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(164)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I do not ask you any reward for it; my reward is only with the Lord of the worlds; \nاَتَاْتُوْنَ الذُّكْرَانَ مِنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(165)\nATAATOONAL AZ-ZUKRAANA MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhat! do you come to the males from among the creatures \nوَ تَذَرُوْنَ مَا خَلَقَ لَكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ مِّنْ اَزْوَاجِكُمْ‌ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ عٰدُوْنَ‏(166)\nWA TAZAROONA MAA KHALAQAL LAKUM RABBOKUM MIN AAZWAAJEKUM BAL ANTUM QAWMUN A’AADOONA.\nAnd leave what your Lord has created for you of your wives? Nay, you are a people exceeding limits. \nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ يٰلُوْطُ لَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُخْرَجِيْنَ‏(167)\nQAALOO LAIL LAM TANTAHE YAALOOTU LATAKOONANNA MENAL AL-MUKHRAJEENA.\nThey said: If you desist not, O Lut! you shall surely be of those who are expelled. \nقَالَ اِنِّىْ لِعَمَلِكُمْ مِّنَ الْقَالِيْنَؕ‏(168)\nQAALA INNEE LEA’AMALEKUM MENAL AL-QAALEENA.\nHe said: Surely I am of those who utterly abhor your \nرَبِّ نَجِّنِىْ وَاَهْلِىْ مِمَّا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(169)\nRABBE NAJJENEE WAAHLEAA MIMMAA YA’MALOON.\nMy Lord! deliver me and my followers from what they do. \nفَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَ اَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(170)\nFANAJJAYNAAHU WA AHLAHU AJMA-E’ENA.\nSo We delivered him and his followers all, \nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(171)\nILLAA A’AJOOZAN FIL GHAABEREEN.\nExcept an old woman, among those who remained behind. \nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(172)\nSUMMA DAMMARNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We utterly destroyed the others. \nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا‌ۚ فَسَآءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(173)\n58 WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM MATARAA FA-SAAA-A MATARUL MUNZEREEN.\nAnd We rained down upon them a rain, and evil was the rain on those warned. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً‌  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(174)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nMost surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(175)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is the Mighty, the Merciful. \nكَذَّبَ اَصْحٰبُ لْئَيْكَةِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ‌ۖ‌ۚ‏(176)\nKAZZABA ASHAABUN LAYKATE MURSALEEN.\nThe dwellers of the thicket gave the lie to the apostles. \nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ شُعَيْبٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(177)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM SHUA’AYBUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen Shu'aib said to them: Will you not guard (against evil)? \nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(178)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUM AMEEN.\nSurely I am a faithful apostle to you; \nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(179)\nFA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nTherefore guard against (the punishment of) Allah and obey me: \nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(180)\nWA MAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAA RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd I do not ask you any reward for it, my reward is only with the Lord of the worlds; \nاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا مِنَ الْمُخْسِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(181)\nAAWFOOA AL-KAYLA WA LAA TAKOONOO MENAL AL-MUKHSEREENA.\nGive a full measure and be not of those who diminish; \nوَزِنُوْا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(182)\nWAZENOOA BIL-QESTAASE AL-MUSTAQEEME.\nAnd weigh (things) with a right balance, \nوَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(183)\nWA LAA TABKHASOOA NAASA AASHYAAAHUM WA LAA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd do not wrong men of their things, and do not act corruptly in the earth, making mischief. \nوَاتَّقُوا الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ وَالْجِبِلَّةَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(184)\nWAT TAQUL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM WAL JEBELLATA AWWALEEN.\nAnd guard against (the punishment of) Him who created you and the former nations. \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِيْنَۙ‏(185)\nQAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MENAL AL-MUSAHHAREENA.\nThey said: You are only of those deluded; \nوَمَاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا وَ اِنْ نَّظُنُّكَ لَمِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(186)\nWA MAA ANTA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA WA IN NNAZUNNUKA LAMENAS KAAZEBEEN.\nAnd you are naught but a mortal like ourselves, and we know you to be certainly of the liars. \nفَاَسْقِطْ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَؕ‏(187)\nFAASQET A’LAYNAA KESAFAN MENAL SAMAAA-E IN KUNTA MENAL AS-SAADEQEENA.\nTherefore cause a portion of the heaven to come down upon us, if you are one of the truthful. \nقَالَ رَبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(188)\nQAALA RABBEE A-A’LAMO BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nHe said: My Lord knows best what you do. \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمِ الظُّلَّةِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(189)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FAAKHAZAHUM A’ZAABO YAWMIL AZ-ZULLATE INNAHU KAANA A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nBut they called him a liar, so the punishment of the day of covering overtook them; surely it was the punishment of a grievous day. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً ‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(190)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAAYATAN WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nMost surely there is a sign in this, but most of them do not believe. \nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(191)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nAnd most surely your Lord is Mighty, the Merciful. \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَتَنْزِيْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(192)\nWA INNAHU LATANZEELU RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd most surely this is a revelation from the Lord of the worlds. \nنَزَلَ بِهِ الرُّوْحُ الْاَمِيْنُۙ‏(193)\nNAZALA BEHIL ROOHO AMEEN.\nThe Faithful Spirit has descended with it, \nعَلٰى قَلْبِكَ لِتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُنْذِرِيْنَۙ‏(194)\nA’LAA QALBEKA LETAKOONA MENAL MUNZEREEN.\nUpon your heart that you may be of the warners \nبِلِسَانٍ عَرَبِىٍّ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(195)\nBELESAANIN A’ARABEAAAIN MMUBEENIN.\nIn plain Arabic language. \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَفِىْ زُبُرِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(196)\nWA INNAHU LAFEE ZUBURE AWWALEEN.\nAnd most surely the same is in the scriptures of the ancients. \nاَوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُمْ اٰيَةً اَنْ يَّعْلَمَهٗ عُلَمٰٓؤُا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(197)\nAWALAM YAKUL LAHUM AAYATAL AN YYAA’LAMAH U’ULAMAAAUA BANEE AESRAAEELA.\nIs it not a sign to them that the learned men of the Israelites know it? \nوَلَوْ نَزَّلْنٰهُ عَلٰى بَعْضِ الْاَعْجَمِيْنَۙ‏(198)\nWA LAW NAZZALNAAHU A’LAA BAA’ZE AL-AAA’JAMEENA.\nAnd if we had revealed it to any of the foreigners \nفَقَرَاَهٗ عَلَيْهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ مُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(199)\nFAQARAAH A’LAYHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI MUMENEENA.\nSo that he should have recited it to them, they would not have believed therein. \nكَذٰلِكَ سَلَكْنٰهُ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَؕ‏(200)\nKAZAALEKA SALAKNAAHU FEE QOLOOBIL AL-MUJREMEENA.\nThus have We caused it to enter into the hearts of the guilty. \nلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَۙ‏(201)\nLAA YOAMENOONA BEHI HATTAA YARAWUA A’ZAABA AL-AALEEMA.\nThey will not believe in it until they see the painful punishment. \nفَيَاْتِيَهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(202)\nFAYAATEEHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nAnd it shall come to them all of a sudden, while they shall not perceive; \nفَيَقُوْلُوْا هَلْ نَحْنُ مُنْظَرُوْنَؕ‏(203)\nFAYAQOOLOO HAL NAHNO MUNZAROONA.\nThen they will say: Shall we be respited? \nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(204)\nAAFABEA’AZAABENAA YASTAA’JELOONA.\nWhat! do they still seek to hasten on Our punishment? \nاَفَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ مَّتَّعْنٰهُمْ سِنِيْنَۙ‏(205)\nAAFARAAYTA IN MMATTAA’NAAHUM SENEEN.\nHave you then considered if We let them enjoy themselves for years, \nثُمَّ جَآءَهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(206)\nSUMMA JAAA-AHUM MAA KAANOO YOOA’ADOONA.\nThen there comes to them that with which they are threatened, \nمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُمَتَّعُوْنَؕ‏(207)\nMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YUMATTAU’OONA.\nThat which they were made to enjoy shall not avail them? \nوَمَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا لَهَا مُنْذِرُوْنَ‌‌‌‌‌ ۛ ‌ۖ ‏(208)\nWA MAA AHLAKNAL MIN QARYATINW ILLAA LAHAA MUNZEROONA.\nAnd We did not destroy any town but it had (its) warners, \nذِكْرٰى‌ۛ وَمَا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(209)\nZEKRAA WA MAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nTo remind, and We are never unjust. \nوَمَا تَنَزَّلَتْ بِهِ الشَّيٰطِيْنُ‏(210)\nWA MAA TANAZZALAT BEHIL SHAYAATEENO.\nAnd the Shaitans have not come down with it. \nوَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَهُمْ وَمَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَؕ‏(211)\nWA MAA LAHAA LAHUM WA MAA YASTATEEU’OONA.\nAnd it behoves them not, and they have not the power to do (it). \nاِنَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّمْعِ لَمَعْزُوْلُوْنَؕ‏(212)\nINNAHUM A’NIL AS-SAME’E LAMAA’ZOOLOONA.\nMost surely they are far removed from the hearing of it. \nفَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(213)\nFALAA TAD-O’ LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FA TAKOONA MENAL AL-MUA’AZZABEENA.\nSo call not upon another god with Allah, lest you be of those who are punished. \nوَاَنْذِرْ عَشِيْرَتَكَ الْاَقْرَبِيْنَۙ‏(214)\nWAANZER A’ASHEERATAKA AL-AAQRABEENA.\nAnd warn your nearest relations, \nوَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِمَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(215)\nWAAKHFEZ JANAAHAKA LEMANIT ATTABAA’AKA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd be kind to him who follows you of the believers. \nفَاِنْ عَصَوْكَ فَقُلْ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(216)\nFA-IN A’ASAWKA FAQUL INNEE BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TA’MALOON.\nBut if they disobey you, then say: Surely I am clear of what you do. \nوَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْعَزِيْزِ الرَّحِيْمِۙ‏(217)\nWA TAWAKKAL A’LAL A’ZEEZIL RAHEEM.\nAnd rely on the Mighty, the Merciful, \nالَّذِىْ يَرٰٮكَ حِيْنَ تَقُوْمُۙ‏(218)\nLAZEE YARAAKA HEENA YAQOOMUS.\nWho sees you when you stand up. \nوَتَقَلُّبَكَ فِى السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(219)\nWATAQALLUBAKA FIL AS-SAAJEDEENA.\nAnd your turning over and over among those who prostrate themselves before Allah. \nاِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(220)\nINNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nSurely He is the Hearing, the Knowing. \nهَلْ اُنَبِّئُكُمْ عَلٰى مَنْ تَنَزَّلُ الشَّيٰطِيْنُؕ‏(221)\nHAL AUNABBEUKUM A’LAA MAN TANAZZALUL ASH-SHAYTEENU.\nShall I inform you (of him) upon whom the Shaitans descend? \nتَنَزَّلُ عَلٰى كُلِّ اَفَّاكٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(222)\nTANAZZALUL A’LAA KULLE AAFFAAKIN ASEEM.\nThey descend upon every lying, sinful one, \nيُّلْقُوْنَ السَّمْعَ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ كٰذِبُوْنَؕ‏(223)\nYYULQOONA JA-A’LA WA AKSAROHUM KAAZEBOONA.\nThey incline their ears, and most of them are liars. \nوَالشُّعَرَآءُ يَتَّبِعُهُمُ الْغَاوٗنَؕ‏(224)\nWAALSSHUA’ARAAU YATTABEU’UHUMU AL-GHAAWNA.\nAnd as to the poets, those who go astray follow them. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّهُمْ فِىْ كُلِّ وَادٍ يَّهِيْمُوْنَۙ‏(225)\nALAM TARA ANNAHUM FEE KULLE WAADIN YYAHEEMOONA.\nDo you not see that they wander about bewildered in every valley? \nوَاَنَّهُمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ مَا لَا يَفْعَلُوْنَۙ‏(226)\nWA ANNAHUM YAQOOLOONA MAA LAA YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd that they say that which they do not do, \nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَذَكَرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا وَّانْتَصَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَسَيَعْلَمُ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَىَّ مُنْقَلَبٍ يَّنْقَلِبُوْنَ‏(227)\nILLAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WAZAKAROOA LAAHA KASEERAA WWAANTASAROOA MIN BA’DE MAA ZULEMOOA WASAYAA’LAMU LAZEENA ZALAMOO AAA MUNQALABIN YYANQALEBOONA.\nExcept those who believe and do good and remember Allah much, and defend themselves after they are oppressed; and they who act unjustly shall know to what final place of turning they shall turn back. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Shoaraa (The Poets)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has a total of 227 verses. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites the three Tawaseen (i.e. the three Surahs beginning with Taa-Seen) on every Thursday night, will be counted from the friends of Allah and will be under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.). The reward for reciting this Surah is so great that when the person sees the reward he has gotten from it (on the Day of Judgement) he will be pleased.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will come out of his grave reciting the Shahadah or Kalimah, bearing witness in the Oneness of Allah (s.w.t.). Reciting Surah al-Shoaraa at dawn is compared to the recitation of all the heavenly books that have been revealed. Frequent recitation of this Surah ensures protection from thieves and from death by drowning or being burnt. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved protects one from all types of ailments."
